      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SO SI GOD (6) ended last campaign with a strong run in tougher company and looks to be at that level judging by her recent trial. Pike hops on board for the resuming effort and the wide draw is no issue. Likely to get back in the run but watch for her flying late in the race. SUNSET SESSION (3) just missed two back before racing in tougher company last start at this track and trip, closing nicely to be 2.9L off the winner. A firmer deck this time suits though and it's important to note he did jump favourite there. Back in grade now and can return to winning ways. SPANISH ARMADA (7) bounced back to score by 2.9L in an impressive front running display at Northam last start when back in trip. He remains at the sprint trips now and he looks a progressive type. Can win again. SHOW ON THE ROAD (5) ended last campaign in good order and can pick up from where he left off. SESH (2) was too good last start and can't be discounted.",
